Z||000000||TRiAD||10-19-2001||11:34 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/bee_fiero.jpg"> <P>Anyone have info on this?<BR>What are the lights/vents in the front fascia and what wing is that?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||10-19-2001||11:46 PM||||I could be wrong about this, but I think it's a Pontiac Concept Show car. If I recall correctly it was in the Auto Museum in Flint MI before they closed it. Haven't seen it surface since that time. Those are lights in the front fascia, you'll notice there are no headlamp doors in the hood.<p>[This message has been edited by California Kid (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||10-20-2001||12:15 AM||||The article says.<BR>"Al Sicz performed the custom modifications to the GT front fascia that incorperates a full set of prototype Sylvania multibeam halogen headlamps that are slated for production use in the near future. Eight lamp openings were cut into the front fascia and lamp pockets were molded in behind each of them.<BR>The stock '87 production headlight covers were glassed-in to enhance the aero look and special rear fascia panel inserts were fabricated to cover the exhaust port tunnels at the back of the car."<P>The wing was made by Art Morrison Enterprises.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||10-20-2001||12:21 AM||||I believe I saw a picture of that car in a magazine recently. One of the guys at a club meeting passed it around and said he wanted to paint his car like that. I think he said it was built by Pontiac as a drag car. One of their experiments or something. If you really want to know I can ask him the next time I see him and get back to you. I'm sure that was the car.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
